The triadic altar configuration is canonically centers: Master Dafeng centred, Huatuo and Hu Tian Yuanshuai flanking laterally. Each deity is identified by its own dark-blue title plaque mounted above the altar, providing iconographic text that makes the identifications explicit:
華陀仙師 | 宋大峰祖師 | 護天元帥

Functional triad — the welfare programme of a Shan Tang
The three deities together encode the comprehensive welfare programme of a Teochew Shan Tang charitable society. Each deity's function corresponds to a domain of charitable provision the institution traditionally addresses:
HUATUO  →  bodily welfare
  Medicine, healing, care of the sick
  The Shan Tang's medical relief programme

MASTER DAFENG  →  social welfare
  Charity, burial of the destitute, founding example
  The Shan Tang's founding charitable mission

HU TIAN YUANSHUAI  →  protective security
  Martial protection, apotropaic warding
  The Shan Tang's protection of the community
This is RFIG's first encounter with a functional welfare triad — a deity configuration where each member corresponds to a distinct functional domain of the institution's charitable work. The triad is iconographically systematic: the institution does not simply venerate Master Dafeng and add other deities at random, but selects deities whose canonical functions correspond to the major activities the institution conducts. Veneration of the altar and the welfare programme of the institution mirror each other.
